PRETABLE ADDENDUM -- #568, written BEFORE kill table 1 runs, after probe REVISION 2 landed (34 rows, md5 19de15b3...;
measured by the probe sub-agent: FIX568 34/34 CONTROL=OK, HEAD 14/34 CONTROL=OK with all 20 population rows
died:exit1, NULL 5/34 CONTROL=FAIL; scratchpad vme/probe/run2_*.out).

== 1. DIFF OF REVISION 2's ROW LIST AGAINST PRETABLE.out's PRESCRIBED ROWS (the #490 rule) ==
  prescribed and present (28): unasm, live, neg apparatus, vbr reset, free ctl, free quiet, cased census, t1cmp rt,
    tctl rt, vbr rt, t1count inc, cased wr, p2 rd census, p2 wr census, p2 ld widths, p2 st widths, p2 ann rd,
    p2 ann wr, p1 fault lo, p1 fault hi, p1 fault wr, p1 census, p1 widths, p1 p2 edge, p2 int byte, p2 int half,
    p3 interim, and the "second passes" -> p2 ann rd 2, p2 ann wr 2 (named rows now)
  RENAMED (1 -> 2): `p2 nonword ann` -> `p2 nw rd` (non-word first READS: ld.bu / ld.hu / ld.d, each announcing its own
    len) + `p2 nw wr` (non-word first WRITES: st.b / st.h / st.d with a 64-bit value whose halves differ).  Every
    prediction PRETABLE.out made for `p2 nonword ann` now names `p2 nw rd` (M_ANNLEN4) and `p2 nw wr` (M_ANNLEN4,
    M_TRUNC).
  ADDED (3): `session` (the control session ran to quit), `free neg ctl` (GCSRCTL's debug line: 1 stepped, 0 free --
    the stepped half proves the match string is right, so the free-running 0 cannot pass by a misspelling),
    `p1 fault mid` (a stepped fault at 0x94, the interior sample).
  DROPPED: none.

== 2. CHANNELS REVISION 2 SAYS CANNOT VARY (recorded before the table, so the table can test the claim) ==
  (i) The read announce's `served` value: every population-2 word is 0 and the first access sets the latch, so a
      variant printing a literal 0 (or idata) instead of odata passes all 34 rows.  Added as leg M_SERVED0, predicted
      to SURVIVE -- an equivalent-today print; disclosed in the contract, beside M_ODATA0.
  (ii) DMT0 / DMA0 in the fault rows are built by the CPU's load/store path before the device is called: they pin
      attribution and CPU behaviour, not the fix; no dev_vme.c leg can move them without also moving PC.
  (iii) Dropping the VBR label reads as CONTROL=FAIL + `nodev` everywhere -- detected, under the device-signature
      reason rather than its own.  Not a leg here (VBR is the signature row's anchor); recorded.

== 3. MEASURED FACTS THE PREDICTIONS NOW REST ON (from revision 2, not from seats) ==
  DMT0: 0x423d word read into r4, 0x433d into r6 (the seat's 0x4000|(dreg<<7)|0x3d confirmed), 0x403f word store,
  0x4211 byte at 1 mod 4, 0x420d halfword at 2 mod 4.  p1 census counts 988/988 with an `addu r1,r1,1; rte` handler.

